        {
            "claim_index": 20,
            "claim": "20. Figure 2: Scale-dependent anisotropy in GraphCast Z500 forecast errors. Each bar group shows the relative power in 3 µ-bins (zonal: µ < 0.33, intermediate: 0.33 ≤ µ < 0.67, meridional: µ ≥ 0.67) for 4 degree bands. Synoptic scales (l = 24–59) show the strongest anisotropy with zonal/meridional ratio of 5.99. Dashed line indicates isotropic reference (33.3 %).",
            "verdict": "Verified",
            "explanation": "Analysis stage: The saved ASED results include the bandwise 3-bin anisotropy weights that underlie the plotted bar groups: `bands = [{l_range:[10,23],weights:[130.31,127.58,31.60],ratio:4.12}, {l_range:[24,59],weights:[5.70,4.31,0.95],ratio:5.99}, ...]`. The 3 equal µ-bins come from `n_mu_bins = 3` in the implementation, and the isotropic reference is the equal-share baseline of 33.3% per bin.",
